Chapter: TruckSpec
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Safari chapter VehicleLimits
  cites Safari chapter World
  cites Safari chapter Truck
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 Truck: the chase. Where it should be, what turn is coming, and the three rules
 that move it one frame.

 THE SCHEDULE IS WHERE IT IS AIMING, NOT WHERE IT IS. It closes from five hundred
 metres ahead down to a hundred by the course end -- not to zero, because the
 point is a photo finish -- and `truck-next` uses it only as the target the free
 rule chases. Grading the schedule at both ends and the middle is what pins the
 lerp; a chapter closing it to zero would look right for most of the course.

 THE ABSENCE OF A TURN IS IN THE TYPE. The zig answers infinity for "no turn" and
 Codex has no literal for that, so `next-turn` answers a `Maybe Turn` -- and the
 terminus answers None rather than a turn of zero, which is the case that decides
 whether the truck brakes as it crosses the finish. Both Nones are graded: past
 the end of the road, and on a segment that terminates.

 THREE RULES, AND THE FLAG BELONGS TO ONE OF THEM. `braking` is a comparison
 against the PREVIOUS speed, not against the intent -- so a truck that wants to
 brake but is already at the caution speed is not braking, and its lights are
 off. That is the distinction graded at the end.

 We say:

Section: The Constants

  fixed-got : List Real
  fixed-got = [start-ahead, finish-lead, truck-turn-caution, truck-brake-distance, truck-max-v]

  fixed-want : List Real
  fixed-want = [500.0, 100.0, 0.8, 60.0, 2.75]

 The chase accelerates a tenth harder than the rider and tops out a tenth faster,
 which is what lets it stay ahead. Neither product is writable as a literal.

  ratio-got : List Real
  ratio-got = [truck-chase-accel, truck-max-v, truck-chase-accel / a-accel, truck-max-v / v-max]

  ratio-want : List Real
  ratio-want = [0.011, 2.75, 1.1, 1.1]

  initial-got : List Real
  initial-got = [truck-initial.pos, truck-initial.v]

  initial-want : List Real
  initial-want = [500.0, 0.3]

  initial-flag-got : List Boolean
  initial-flag-got = [truck-initial.braking]

  initial-flag-want : List Boolean
  initial-flag-want = [False]

Section: The Schedule

 At the start it wants to be five hundred ahead; at the line, a hundred. Halfway
 down a thousand-metre course it wants three hundred.

  sched-got : List Real
  sched-got =
    [ truck-schedule 0.0 1000.0,
      truck-schedule 250.0 1000.0,
      truck-schedule 500.0 1000.0,
      truck-schedule 1000.0 1000.0,
      truck-schedule 1000.0 1000.0 - 1000.0,
      truck-schedule 0.0 1000.0 - 0.0 ]

  sched-want : List Real
  sched-want = [500.0, 650.0, 800.0, 1100.0, 100.0, 500.0]

Section: The Next Turn

 One segment, five hundred long, with a fifty-degree exit. Anywhere on it the
 turn is at the far end and the safe speed is the table's.

  one-seg : List Segment
  one-seg = [segment-at 0]

  turn-dist : List Segment, Real -> Real
  turn-dist (segs) (pos) =
    when next-turn segs pos
     is Just (t) -> t.dist
     is None -> 0.0 - 1.0

  turn-v : List Segment, Real -> Real
  turn-v (segs) (pos) =
    when next-turn segs pos
     is Just (t) -> t.v-turn
     is None -> 0.0 - 1.0

  turn-got : List Real
  turn-got =
    [ turn-dist one-seg 0.0, turn-dist one-seg 450.0, turn-dist one-seg 499.0,
      turn-v one-seg 0.0, turn-v one-seg 450.0,
      turn-speed (list-at one-seg 0).exit-angle ]

  turn-want : List Real
  turn-want = [500.0, 50.0, 1.0, 0.222, 0.222, 0.222]

 Past the end of the road there is no turn, and neither is there one on the
 segment that terminates -- a None rather than a turn of zero.

  none-got : List Real
  none-got =
    [ turn-dist one-seg 500.0,
      turn-dist one-seg 900.0,
      turn-dist [segment-at 18] 0.0,
      turn-dist [] 0.0 ]

  none-want : List Real
  none-want = [-1.0, -1.0, -1.0, -1.0]

 A chain of two: the first turn is still the first segment's, and past it the
 second segment's own.

  two-seg : List Segment
  two-seg = [segment-at 0, segment-at 1]

  chain-got : List Real
  chain-got =
    [ turn-dist two-seg 0.0, turn-dist two-seg 500.0, turn-dist two-seg 800.0,
      turn-dist two-seg 820.0 ]

  chain-want : List Real
  chain-want = [500.0, 320.0, 20.0, -1.0]

Section: One Frame

 Behind schedule and far from the turn, it accelerates by the chase rate and
 moves by the new speed.

  free : TruckState
  free = truck-next (TruckState { pos = 100.0, v = 0.3, braking = False }) 0.0 one-seg 1000.0

  free-got : List Real
  free-got = [free.v, free.pos, free.v - 0.3]

  free-want : List Real
  free-want = [0.311, 100.311, 0.011]

 Ahead of schedule it holds its speed rather than coasting down, and it still
 moves. At the start the schedule is 500, so 600 is ahead of it and 400 is
 behind -- both are graded, because the rule is a comparison and it is the only
 thing separating them.

  ahead : TruckState
  ahead = truck-next (TruckState { pos = 600.0, v = 0.5, braking = False }) 0.0 one-seg 1000.0

  behind : TruckState
  behind = truck-next (TruckState { pos = 400.0, v = 0.5, braking = False }) 0.0 one-seg 1000.0

  ahead-got : List Real
  ahead-got = [ahead.v, ahead.pos, behind.v - ahead.v]

  ahead-want : List Real
  ahead-want = [0.5, 600.5, 0.011]

 The top speed is a cap and not a target: a truck already at it stays there.

  capped : TruckState
  capped = truck-next (TruckState { pos = 100.0, v = truck-max-v, braking = False }) 0.0 one-seg 1000.0

  capped-got : List Real
  capped-got = [capped.v]

  capped-want : List Real
  capped-want = [2.75]

  free-flag-got : List Boolean
  free-flag-got = [free.braking, ahead.braking, capped.braking]

  free-flag-want : List Boolean
  free-flag-want = [False, False, False]

Section: Braking

 Inside the brake distance the kinematic rule takes over, arriving at the turn at
 four fifths of the safe speed. It is recomputed every frame, so it tracks rather
 than committing.

  braking : TruckState
  braking = truck-next (TruckState { pos = 450.0, v = 0.3, braking = False }) 0.0 one-seg 1000.0

  brake-got : List Real
  brake-got = [braking.v, braking.pos - 450.0]

  brake-want : List Real
  brake-want = [0.2994154176, 0.2994154176]

  brake-flag-got : List Boolean
  brake-flag-got = [braking.braking, braking.v < 0.3, braking.v > 0.1776]

  brake-flag-want : List Boolean
  brake-flag-want = [True, True, True]

 THE LIGHTS ARE OFF WHEN IT IS NOT ACTUALLY SLOWING. A truck already at the
 caution speed inside the brake zone cannot go slower, so the flag is False even
 though the braking rule is the one that ran.

  settled : TruckState
  settled = truck-next (TruckState { pos = 450.0, v = 0.1776, braking = True }) 0.0 one-seg 1000.0

  settled-got : List Boolean
  settled-got = [settled.braking, settled.v ~0 0.1776]

  settled-want : List Boolean
  settled-want = [False, True]

 Just outside the brake distance it is still free, and just inside it is not --
 the boundary is `<=`, so a turn exactly sixty metres off brakes.

  boundary-got : List Boolean
  boundary-got =
    [ (truck-next (TruckState { pos = 440.0, v = 0.3, braking = False }) 0.0 one-seg 1000.0).v < 0.3,
      (truck-next (TruckState { pos = 439.0, v = 0.3, braking = False }) 0.0 one-seg 1000.0).v < 0.3 ]

  boundary-want : List Boolean
  boundary-want = [True, False]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-fixed " fixed-got fixed-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-ratio " ratio-got ratio-want 0.000000000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-init  " initial-got initial-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "tk-iflag " initial-flag-got initial-flag-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-sched " sched-got sched-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-turn  " turn-got turn-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-none  " none-got none-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-chain " chain-got chain-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-free  " free-got free-want 0.000000000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-ahead " ahead-got ahead-want 0.000000000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-cap   " capped-got capped-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "tk-fflag " free-flag-got free-flag-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tk-brake " brake-got brake-want 0.000000000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "tk-bflag " brake-flag-got brake-flag-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "tk-settle" settled-got settled-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "tk-bound " boundary-got boundary-want)
  end
